INSERT INTO part (id, message_id, session_id, time_created, time_updated, data) VALUES ('prt_0007', 'msg_0005', 'opencode-real-sanitized', 1786708803506, 1786708803506, '{"text":"The user wants to build a cross-Coding-Agent history migration tool. This is a real software engineering task. Let me think about what they need. They describe: - Background: They switch between Codex, OpenCode, Pi Agent coding agents - Core: Complete handoff of execution history (conversations/reasoning + tool call traces) to another agent - Boundary: What survives in workspace (files, state) doesn''t need migration; what''s in session (conversation, tool traces) needs migration - Functional needs: 1. Read: parse Codex/OpenCode/Pi Agent local history, extract conversations + tool call records 2. Export: structured portable execution trace (unified data model) 3. Import/seed: seed the trace into new agent as starting context - Architecture: Compiler/translator style, each agent has an adapter component, each converts to a unified intermediate structure (IR), then to another agent format → n adapters total This is a substantial project. The working directory is /home/user/WORKSPACE/migrate. Let me check what''s there. It''s not a git repo. I should first explore the working directory to see if there''s anything there already. Then discuss the design and ask clarifying questions before building. Let me check the environment first. The directory is /home/user/WORKSPACE/migrate. Let me look at what''s there. Given the scope, I should: 1. Explore current directory state 2. Ask clarifying questions about key decisions (language, which agent''s storage format they have access to, how to seed into OpenCode which is the current agent, etc.) Actually the user is running this from within opencode. OpenCode itself stores session history locally. So they want to migrate between agents. Let me think about the key design questions: - What language? (Go, Rust, TypeScript?) - What''s the actual storage format for each agent? (I know OpenCode uses ~/.local/share/opencode or similar with JSON storage. Codex uses ~/.codex/sessions or ~/.codex/history as JSONL. Pi Agent - I''d need to check.) - \n[TRUNCATED]","time":{"end":1786708809599,"start":1786708803506},"type":"reasoning"}');
