INSERT INTO part (id, message_id, session_id, time_created, time_updated, data) VALUES ('prt_0039', 'msg_0011', 'opencode-real-sanitized', 1786708830232, 1786708830232, '{"text":"Now I have a clear picture of the three formats: 1. **OpenCode**: SQLite DB. `session` → `message` (role) → `part` (text/tool/reasoning/step-start/step-finish). Part data has a `type` field. 2. **Codex**: JSONL rollout. Types: `session_meta`, `event_msg`, `response_item`, `turn_context`. Need to check the response_item structure for tool calls. 3. **Pi Agent**: JSONL. Types: `session`, `model_change`, `thinking_level_change`, `message`. Message has role user/assistant with content array (text). Need to see how tool calls appear in Pi - maybe in content array as function_call/function_call_output. Let me dig a bit more into the tool formats of each so I can design a good IR. Let me check: - OpenCode tool part data structure - Codex response_item structure - Pi agent - does it have tool calls? Let me search a bigger Pi session. The AgentScout ones seem short. Let me check the -home-user-- ones which might be longer. Actually, this is getting deep into research. The user has given me a clear requirements doc and an architecture sketch (compiler/translator with n adapters). The directory is empty. I think the right move now is: 1. Confirm the plan and gather a couple of key decisions from the user (language choice, target agent priority, how seeding should work). 2. Then build an initial scaffold. Actually, let me think about what high-leverage questions to ask: 1. **Language / runtime**: The tool reads local histories, exports a portable trace, and seeds into new agents. It needs to write into target agent''s storage (e.g., inject a message into OpenCode''s DB, or generate an importable session file). TypeScript/Node makes sense since OpenCode and Codex CLI are both Node-ish (Codex CLI is Rust actually, but config JSON). Python is also viable. Since user is running opencode (Node-based) and has bun, node available. I''ll ask. 2. **Seeding mechanism for the target agent**: This is the crux. Options: - a) Directly write into target''s storage format (e.g., insert message/par\n[TRUNCATED]","time":{"end":1786708839297,"start":1786708830231},"type":"reasoning"}');
