INSERT INTO part (id, message_id, session_id, time_created, time_updated, data) VALUES ('prt_0070', 'msg_0017', 'opencode-real-sanitized', 1786709910524, 1786709910524, '{"text":"The user chose: 1. **Rust** for implementation 2. **Dual mode** (write to native storage + output structured seed file), and importantly: they want the tool to actively check whether the seed file''s corresponding content (both original agent session and target session) has changed, and sync. This is a \"diff/sync\" feature. 3. **Read all + export + one target import** milestone. So the plan: **Milestone 1 (this session):** - Rust CLI tool - IR (intermediate representation) — unified data model - Readers: Codex, OpenCode, Pi Agent → IR - Exporter: IR → structured portable seed file (e.g., JSON + Markdown transcript) - Importer: IR/seed → OpenCode (native injection into SQLite) - Sync/diff check: verify original session and target session state, detect changes Let me think about the architecture: ``` migrate/ ├── Cargo.toml ├── src/ │ ├── main.rs # CLI entry (clap) │ ├── ir.rs # unified data model │ ├── readers/ │ │ ├── mod.rs │ │ ├── codex.rs # JSONL rollout reader │ │ ├── opencode.rs # SQLite reader │ │ └── pi.rs # Pi Agent JSONL reader │ ├── export/ │ │ ├── mod.rs │ │ ├── seed.rs # structured seed file (JSON + markdown) │ │ └── markdown.rs # human-readable transcript │ └── import/ │ ├── mod.rs │ └── opencode.rs # inject into OpenCode SQLite │ └── sync.rs # change detection / diff ``` **IR design** (unified data model): ```rust struct Trace { source: AgentMeta, // agent type, version, session id, cwd entries: Vec<Entry>, } struct Entry { time: Option<DateTime>, kind: EntryKind, } enum EntryKind { UserMessage { text: Vec<ContentBlock> }, AssistantMessage { text: Vec<ContentBlock> }, Reasoning { text: String }, // chain of thought ToolCall { id: String, name: String, arguments: Value }, ToolResult { call_id: String, output: String, exit_code: Option<i32>, error: Option<String> }, ModelChange { provider, model }, } ``` Actually, to preserve ordering and pairing, I''ll use a flat event stream with optional call_id pairing. Each agent reader produces the same IR event strea\n[TRUNCATED]","time":{"end":1786709921767,"start":1786709910524},"type":"reasoning"}');
