INSERT INTO part (id, message_id, session_id, time_created, time_updated, data) VALUES ('prt_0160', 'msg_0041', 'opencode-real-sanitized', 1786710042710, 1786710042710, '{"text":"Now the OpenCode reader (SQLite). Format: - session table: id, project_id, directory, title, model, time_created, time_updated - message table: id, session_id, role in data (json_extract(data,''$.role'')), time_created - part table: message_id, session_id, data For a given session, query messages ordered by time_created, then parts per message ordered by time_created. Part data types: - text: {type, text} - tool: {type, tool, callID, state:{status, input, output, metadata:{exit, truncated}, time}} - reasoning: {type, text} - step-start/step-finish: ignore (or could map? ignore for now) Mapping: - message role user → UserMessage (text from text parts) - message role assistant → text parts → AssistantMessage; reasoning parts → Reasoning; tool parts → ToolCall + ToolResult. A tool part contains both input (call) and output (result) in one part. I''ll emit a ToolCall then a ToolResult immediately (with same timestamp), pairing by callID. For the tool part: - ToolCall {id: callID, name: tool, arguments: JSON of state.input} - ToolResult {call_id: callID, output: state.output, exit_code: state.metadata.exit, error: Some if status==\"error\"} Let me write opencode.rs.","time":{"end":1786710044829,"start":1786710042710},"type":"reasoning"}');
