INSERT INTO part (id, message_id, session_id, time_created, time_updated, data) VALUES ('prt_0178', 'msg_0045', 'opencode-real-sanitized', 1786710077210, 1786710077210, '{"text":"Now I understand the project schema. `worktree` is the path. For import: 1. Find project by worktree = cwd (or create one). 2. Create a session row (need unique id — uuid v4; I don''t have a uuid crate. Let me generate a uuid-like id from random bytes via a simple approach, or add `uuid` crate. Adding uuid crate is cleaner. Let me add it to Cargo.toml). 3. Insert messages with data `{\"role\": ...}` and parts with data of each type. 4. Message/part ids also need unique ids — uuid. Let me add the uuid crate. The message.data can include `time:{created}`. Let me keep minimal: `{\"role\":\"user\"}`. That''s what OpenCode writes minimally. Actually to be safe I''ll include role only. Parts: - text: `{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"...\"}` - reasoning: `{\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"text\":\"...\"}` - tool: `{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":name,\"callID\":id,\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":<args parsed>,\"output\":\"...\",\"metadata\":{\"exit\":code,\"truncated\":false},\"time\":{\"start\":ts,\"end\":ts}}}` For grouping into messages: The importer should group events into messages. I''ll create: - For each UserMessage/AssistantMessage → a message with that role + a text part. - For Reasoning → attach as reasoning part to the preceding assistant message (or create an assistant message for it if none). - For ToolCall → create an assistant message (if no pending assistant message) with a tool part (the tool part contains both call+result in OpenCode, so one part per ToolCall+ToolResult pair). Actually OpenCode stores tool as a single part with state containing input and output. So I should pair ToolCall with its following ToolResult, then emit one part. But simpler and more robust: create one assistant \"message\" per tool invocation that contains a tool part. And user/assistant text messages as separate messages. The anchor message id for sync: the last message we insert. Let me design the importer: ```rust pub struct ImportResult { pub session_id: String, pub anchor_message_id: String, pub message_count: usize } pub fn import(\n[TRUNCATED]","time":{"end":1786710083517,"start":1786710077210},"type":"reasoning"}');
