INSERT INTO part (id, message_id, session_id, time_created, time_updated, data) VALUES ('prt_0186', 'msg_0047', 'opencode-real-sanitized', 1786710090593, 1786710090593, '{"text":"The \"global\" project has worktree `/`. So for a specific directory, I should find a project by worktree = directory, and if not found, either reuse \"global\" or create a new project. To keep it simple and safe: if a project with matching worktree exists, use it; otherwise use the \"global\" project (worktree=\"/\") — that''s what OpenCode does for ad-hoc. Actually, simpler and more correct: use the project matching the cwd, else fall back to \"global\". Now for session id: I''ll use the uuid crate to generate. Actually OpenCode ids are `ses_` prefix + something. For a synthetic import, any unique text id works. I''ll generate with uuid v4 and prefix `ses_`. Let me add uuid crate. Message ids: OpenCode uses `msg_...`. Part ids `prt_...`. I''ll use `msg_<uuid>` and `prt_<uuid>`. Let me add uuid crate to Cargo.toml. Now let me write the importer. I''ll also handle the transaction properly with rusqlite. For slug: OpenCode slugs are like \"swift-rocket\" (random word). I''ll just use a short hash or a word like \"imported\". Let me write import/opencode.rs. Key detail: message.data — I''ll write `{\"role\":\"user\",\"time\":{\"created\":<ts>}}`. part.data for tool needs state JSON. Let me write it now. Also need `version` in session — set to opencode current version string like \"1.18.18\" or something benign. I''ll use \"1.18.18\" to match current... actually that''s fragile. Let me just use \"0.0.0\"? It may confuse the UI. Better to read the max version from existing sessions. Simpler: query one existing session''s version. I''ll do `SELECT version FROM session LIMIT 1`. Let me write the importer code.","time":{"end":1786710094762,"start":1786710090593},"type":"reasoning"}');
