INSERT INTO part (id, message_id, session_id, time_created, time_updated, data) VALUES ('prt_0197', 'msg_0050', 'opencode-real-sanitized', 1786710115825, 1786710115825, '{"text":"Now the sync module. The `status` command: - Load manifest from out_dir. - Re-read the source: for codex/pi, re-read the source file and compute its sha256 + events hash. Compare with manifest.source.file_sha256 and events_sha256. - Check the target: if manifest.target is Some, read the target opencode session (need db path) and check: - The anchor message still exists. - Are there messages after the anchor? If yes, the target agent continued beyond the seed point. - If the session or anchor is missing → target changed/replaced. For re-reading the source, I need to know its kind from manifest.source.agent. Then: - codex: file is path; read file, compute hash. - pi: same. - opencode: file is `path(session_id)`; re-open db and read. Actually for the sync check on source, comparing file hash of the raw file is the primary signal (did the source session change). For opencode the \"file\" is virtual (db). I''ll recompute the events hash from re-reading via the reader. Let me define a StatusReport: ```rust pub struct SourceStatus { pub unchanged: bool, pub detail: String } pub struct TargetStatus { pub present: bool, pub continued_past_seed: bool, pub extra_messages: usize, pub detail: String } pub struct StatusReport { pub manifest, pub source: SourceStatus, pub target: TargetStatus } ``` For re-reading source, I''ll reuse readers::read_trace with agent kind. The `session` arg for codex/pi: the manifest.source.file is the full path, so read_trace with the file path directly (resolve_session_file accepts existing files). For opencode, pass session_id and db path. For target status, I need db path. The status command takes `--db` optional override for opencode (default ~/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db). Query: count messages in target session where time_created > anchor''s time_created OR id ordering after anchor. Simpler: get anchor message''s time_created, then count messages with time_created > that, or count messages after anchor id in the ordered sequence. I''ll query mes\n[TRUNCATED]","time":{"end":1786710124070,"start":1786710115825},"type":"reasoning"}');
