INSERT INTO part (id, message_id, session_id, time_created, time_updated, data) VALUES ('prt_0284', 'msg_0073', 'opencode-real-sanitized', 1786710244271, 1786710244271, '{"text":"The round-trip events hash is `6cab512d...` vs original `c701d9f2...`. They differ. Why? The original Pi trace had 332 events, roundtrip has 331. Difference of 1. Probably a `ModelChange` event. In the Pi reader, `model_change` events are emitted as events. But when importing, ModelChange events are ignored (skipped). The source Pi file had 12 model_change events, but only some get emitted... wait, in the Pi reader, every `model_change` line emits a ModelChange event. So the source has N model_change events. On import I skip them, so the roundtrip loses all model_change events. Source: 332 events. Roundtrip: 331. So difference is 1... that''s odd, if all model_change events were skipped the difference would be more. Let me check how many ModelChange events are in the source. Actually wait — in the Pi reader, the `model_change` event handler: `meta.model = ...; events.push(ModelChange)`. Every model_change line creates an event. Let me count.","time":{"end":1786710246286,"start":1786710244271},"type":"reasoning"}');
