INSERT INTO part (id, message_id, session_id, time_created, time_updated, data) VALUES ('prt_0289', 'msg_0074', 'opencode-real-sanitized', 1786710249105, 1786710249105, '{"text":"As suspected: the source has 1 `model_change` event (the Pi session had one model_change line that was emitted — actually there were 2 model_change lines in the file but only 1 got... no, source shows 1 model_change). The importer skips ModelChange events, so the roundtrip lost it. Question: should the importer persist ModelChange? It''s meta-ish. OpenCode stores model on the session row, not per-message. We could set the session''s model to the last model. That''s reasonable — the roundtrip would then have matching events if we don''t emit model_change from the imported session... but then re-exporting wouldn''t reproduce the model_change event, so hash still differs. Options: 1. Emit model_change events as their own \"assistant\" messages? No — hacky. 2. Accept the hash difference but note that model_change is a source-only event. The sync \"events unchanged\" check for the target isn''t about matching source hash exactly — it''s about detecting whether the target changed after seeding. So the target events hash in manifest being different from source events hash is fine; the sync check for the target compares anchor position and presence, not hash equality to source. Actually, look at sync.check: for the target, `check_target` doesn''t compare hashes — it checks session presence, anchor presence, and extra messages after anchor. Good. The events_sha256 in TargetRef is informational. But there''s an important subtlety for roundtrip integrity: if the user later re-exports the imported session to migrate again to another agent, losing the model_change is acceptable (it''s minor metadata). And the tool part pairing is preserved. Text preserved. Reasoning preserved. So roundtrip is ~complete. However — one concern: my roundtrip reader produced the same event counts except model_change. That''s a clean result. But wait, there''s a subtle ordering issue in the importer for assistant text + reasoning + tool calls: In the source Pi session, the assistant message content order was [thinki\n[TRUNCATED]","time":{"end":1786710258126,"start":1786710249105},"type":"reasoning"}');
