INSERT INTO part (id, message_id, session_id, time_created, time_updated, data) VALUES ('prt_0303', 'msg_0077', 'opencode-real-sanitized', 1786710269655, 1786710269655, '{"text":"The Codex round-trip is **perfect** — 93 events identical to source (19 assistant, 32 tool_call, 32 tool_result, 10 user_message). No reasoning events in this codex session (interesting — the codex reader''s `reasoning` only emits if there''s `summary` text; this session''s reasoning items may have `encrypted_content` or empty summary). The tool pairing works correctly. Note: codex source had 93 events and roundtrip 93 events. But the events hash differs (`47b1e...` vs `7161...`). Why? The tool part in OpenCode: I store arguments as parsed JSON value in `state.input`, then re-read it via `serde_json::to_string(&input)` — that should be stable JSON. But the ordering could differ? Actually the issue: in the codex source, `arguments` is a JSON string `{\"cmd\":\"...\",\"workdir\":\"...\",\"max_output_tokens\":4000,\"yield_time_ms\":1000}`. When imported, I parse it to Value and store. On re-read, I serialize the stored Value → same key order preserved by serde_json (Value uses BTreeMap? No, serde_json::Value Map is IndexMap which preserves insertion order by default in serde_json). Actually serde_json preserves order as read. So hash should match... unless the output text differs or something. Wait, the difference: in the source codex, `arguments` includes all keys. On roundtrip, the re-read produces the same arguments. Hmm, but maybe the difference is the `time` field or `exit_code`? No, those are null in codex. Actually, let me check what differs. The events hash differs. Possible causes: 1. Tool result output: codex `output` is a string; preserved. 2. Maybe there are reasoning items in codex with summary — but count shows no reasoning events in either. 3. The `arguments` string: in codex source it''s exactly the JSON string from the file. After roundtrip through OpenCode, I store parsed Value and re-serialize. serde_json::to_string(Value) uses compact form without spaces: `{\"cmd\":\"rg --files\",\"workdir\":...}`. The original from codex was `{\"cmd\":\"rg --files\",\"workdir\":...}` — also c\n[TRUNCATED]","time":{"end":1786710278404,"start":1786710269655},"type":"reasoning"}');
INSERT INTO part (id, message_id, session_id, time_created, time_updated, data) VALUES ('prt_0304', 'msg_0077', 'opencode-real-sanitized', 1786710278406, 1786710278406, '{"text":"Codex round-trip is 1:1 on counts (93 events, tool pairing correct). Two things to check: (1) Codex reasoning items aren''t being extracted — let me verify the field name, and (2) confirm the events-hash diff is only cosmetic (JSON key ordering).","time":{"end":1786710280049,"start":1786710278405},"type":"text"}');
