INSERT INTO part (id, message_id, session_id, time_created, time_updated, data) VALUES ('prt_0435', 'msg_0111', 'opencode-real-sanitized', 1786752840353, 1786752840353, '{"text":"Now need update main.rs. We need: - Add `use migrate::config;`. - Export `out: Option<PathBuf>` not required. Clap `#[arg(short,long)] out: Option<PathBuf>`. - Import seed should be optional? The user asked why migrate must specify target directory. There are two places: export output dir (`-o`) and import seed dir (`--seed`). The specific \"target directory\" likely export out. But \"config file/env var default directory\" should apply to both export and import/status default seed. Maybe `--seed` can also be optional: `Import { seed: Option<PathBuf> }`, `Status { seed: Option<PathBuf> }` with default to `MIGRATE_SEED_DIR`? But if no `--seed` and there are multiple seeds, which seed? Need avoid ambiguity. For import/status, a default \"current seed dir\" can be the base directory, not a specific seed path. That''s not enough. Unless we use the latest seed in the default seed base. That might be useful: `latest_seed_dir()` scans base recursively for manifest.json and picks most recently modified. But might surprise. The user wants config/env to default specify directory. This could mean a base seed dir. For export, no target dir needed. For import/status, still need `--seed` or we can default to the most recent seed path. Hmm. I think implement: - `export`: `-o` optional; if omitted, uses `default_seed_output(agent, trace.meta.session_id)`. - `import` and `status`: `--seed` optional. If omitted, use `MIGRATE_SEED_DIR` as the seed dir **only if it contains seed.json/manifest.json**, otherwise use the most recent manifest under the seed base. This could be convenient. But perhaps too much? The user said \"用一个配置文件，或者说环境变量来默认指定目录\" — likely for seed directory. So import/status can default to `default_seed_dir()` if it''s a concrete seed directory. But if default_seed_dir is a base, not a seed, status fails with \"missing manifest\". Better to implement latest resolution. Let me add functions in config: - `resolve_seed_dir(seed: Option<PathBuf>) -> Result<PathBuf, String>`? Should li\n[TRUNCATED]","time":{"end":1786752855791,"start":1786752840353},"type":"text"}');
