INSERT INTO part (id, message_id, session_id, time_created, time_updated, data) VALUES ('prt_0538', 'msg_0132', 'opencode-real-sanitized', 1786753316450, 1786753316450, '{"text":"Good. Now maybe update command help text? `Export` says `-o` optional but Clap will show optional. Fine. But the `Status` command takes a positional `seed: Option<PathBuf>`. It is not named `--seed`, unlike import has --seed. The previous status was positional. Now optional positional, so `migrate status` works. Good. But import''s `--seed` optional still requires named flag. Can users pass positional seed? No. Current command: ``` Import { agent, #[arg(short,long)] seed: Option<PathBuf> } ``` Usage: `migrate import <agent> [OPTIONS]`. This is fine. Question: \"为什么 Migrate 要指定目标目录，我们是不是用一个配置文件...\" I should mention no longer required: - `migrate export pi <session>` now defaults to env/config seed directory. - Config env var: - `MIGRATE_SEED_DIR=/path/to/seeds` - `MIGRATE_CONFIG=/path/config.json` - default config path `~/.config/migrate/config.json` with `{\"seed_dir\":\"~/...\"}` - If omitted import/status finds latest seed under default seed base. Need maybe ensure path expansion for `MIGRATE_CONFIG`? It doesn''t expand ~ for config path. Only seed_dir. Okay. Need maybe add tests for `config::default_seed_output`? Environment variable in tests is unsafe now? In Rust 2024, setting env in tests is unsafe? Actually std::env::set_var is unsafe in edition 2024? Hmm not needed. Now update final after running `cargo test` and clippy. Need maybe run `git status` to summarize files changed. Use bash git status.","time":{"end":1786753321158,"start":1786753316450},"type":"text"}');
