INSERT INTO part (id, message_id, session_id, time_created, time_updated, data) VALUES ('prt_0572', 'msg_0140', 'opencode-real-sanitized', 1786753947803, 1786753947803, '{"text":"Need real conversion tests. We should not touch real DB. Use temp seeds and DB copy / Pi temp root. Need select real session IDs. Use earlier known: - Pi real rich session: `2026-08-10T15-20-56-187Z_019fec43-...` or use first list. Use the one with rich tool calls. - OpenCode real session: `ses_fffdc21c6ffeXQDzCkQedxDLgn` maybe current session. We can export real OpenCode to seed and import to Pi temp root or opencode copy. Need test at least: 1. Real Pi session → export seed → import OpenCode (DB copy) → status 2. Real Pi session → export seed → import Pi (temp root) → status 3. Real OpenCode session → export seed → import Pi (temp root) → status maybe. 4. Real OpenCode session → export seed → import OpenCode copy? This tests OpenCode reader and importer from OpenCode to OpenCode. The user specifically asks \"真实的 pi session 和 Open Code session 进行转换测试吗？也不一定是就是这两个 session，也可能是其他 session 进行转换，都有测试吗？\" We should do smoke tests across real Pi/OpenCode sessions. Let''s do four combos? Could be time manageable. Need avoid writing real Pi root for smoke. Use `--pi-root /tmp/real-pi-import-root`. Need avoid writing real OpenCode DB. Use copied db with `--opencode-db /tmp/...`. Commands: - prep: rm dirs; cp real opencode db to temp. - Test 1 real Pi → OpenCode copy: ``` MIGRATE_SEED_DIR=/tmp/migrate-real-pi-to-open ./target/debug/migrate export pi <pi-id> ... import opencode --opencode-db /tmp/db/opencode.db ... status --opencode-db /tmp/db/opencode.db ``` - Test 2 real Pi → Pi temp: But reusing same seed dir after importing opencode updates manifest.target to opencode; to test Pi, use separate seed dir. - Test 3 real OpenCode → Pi: ``` MIGRATE_SEED_DIR=/tmp/migrate-real-open-to-pi ./target/debug/migrate export opencode <opencode-id> --opencode-db copy? Actually exporting reads real DB. Read-only is fine. Could use real DB or copy. Use copy to avoid DB locks? For current opencode DB read is okay. Use copy to avoid variation. Use `--opencode-db /tmp/db/opencode.db`. import pi --\n[TRUNCATED]","time":{"end":1786753956751,"start":1786753947803},"type":"text"}');
