INSERT INTO part (id, message_id, session_id, time_created, time_updated, data) VALUES ('prt_0621', 'msg_0153', 'opencode-real-sanitized', 1786757037067, 1786757037067, '{"text":"Sanitizer missed nested keys in Codex event_msg changes: map keys are file paths in object keys, not values, and unified_diff contains paths in key? Actually grep found map keys as `\"/home/user/...\":` — sanitize_value doesn''t sanitize object keys. Need sanitize keys too, particularly object maps with path keys. This is sensitive. Need update Sanitizer to sanitize object keys; but if we change all keys, it might break schema keys (id/type/payload). Need only if key contains home or WORKSPACE/user maybe. For object maps: - Create new map with sanitized key if needed: ```rust let keys: Vec<String>=map.keys().cloned().collect(); for old in keys { let new=sanitize_key(&old); if new != old { if let Some(v)=map.remove(&old) { map.insert(new,v); } } } ``` Need `serde_json::Map` order? OK. In sanitize key call `sanitize_text` but might truncate long. For path keys OK. Also there are literal session filenames etc. We don''t need remove? They are feature-ish but not sensitive maybe. But we might want to redact ids in text values that show session id etc. The user asked feature info too, but not everything. Good. Grep second found `token` false positives (rate_limit type not sensitive), but \"api key\" from Pi error? Need ensure actual keys redacted. Search for specific invalid API key pattern maybe. `[REDACTED_API_KEY]-REDACTED-` present is okay? But grep returned `[REDACTED_API_KEY]-` from redacted, which is not a real key but still maybe ok. We can turn to `[REDACTED_API_KEY]` instead of `[REDACTED_API_KEY]-REDACTED-` to avoid grep. Patch sanitize_text. Also `encrypted_content` is redacted. Need maybe not include huge fixtures? But okay. After patch, rerun generator.","time":{"end":1786757044911,"start":1786757037067},"type":"text"}');
