INSERT INTO part (id, message_id, session_id, time_created, time_updated, data) VALUES ('prt_0631', 'msg_0155', 'opencode-real-sanitized', 1786757122632, 1786757122632, '{"text":"No matches. Need include tests that use real fixtures. Current tests only use simple fixtures, not new sanitized fixtures. Add tests: - `sanitized_real_pi_fixture_parses`: read tests/fixtures/real/pi_real_sanitized.jsonl assert >50 events with model, tool, result, reasoning. - `sanitized_real_codex_fixture_parses`: read codex real assert has tool calls/results and messages. - `sanitized_real_opencode_sql_fixture_parses`: Create temp DB schema, execute SQL, read session id `opencode-real-sanitized`, assert events >20 and has tool/reasoning. Need maybe check codex reader handles this particular codex fixture event types. The picked codex may use `custom_tool_call` / `custom_tool_call_output` not `function_call`? Earlier real sanitized codex seemed payload name exec type custom_tool_call and output type custom_tool_call_output maybe. Our codex reader only parses `function_call`, `function_call_output`, `message`, `reasoning`. So test may expose missing coverage. Good! Let me run quickly reading using CLI export codex fixture? Use `./migrate export codex tests/fixtures/real/codex_real_sanitized.jsonl`.","time":{"end":1786757125526,"start":1786757122632},"type":"text"}');
